# Line endings.
#
# SCOPED DELIBERATELY TO styles/. That directory is HASH-PINNED:
# styles/Taste/STYLE_SOURCE.json records a SHA-256 per vendored rule. Without an
# eol rule Git checks those files out with CRLF on Windows and LF elsewhere, so
# the digests describe bytes that exist on one runner and not the other. Measured:
# PR #197 passed `validator (ubuntu-latest)` and failed `validator (windows-latest)`
# with all six digests mismatched and nothing wrong with the files.
#
# A hash over a text file must not depend on the platform that checked it out.
styles/** text eol=lf

# WHY THIS FILE DOES NOT PIN THE WHOLE REPOSITORY, THOUGH IT SHOULD EVENTUALLY.
#
# Ten tracked files currently hold CRLF in the index:
#
#   .claude-plugin/marketplace.json          scripts/validate_conformance.py
#   SECURITY.md                              scripts/validate_eval_corpora.py
#   dispositions/2026-08-15-S295-admission-triage.md
#   skills/engineering/git-pull-rebase-trap/SKILL.md
#   skills/engineering/im-down/test_validate_packet.py
#   skills/engineering/im-up/test_validate_packet.py
#   skills/orchestration/parallel-review-disposition-schema/SKILL.md
#   skills/orchestration/parallel-review-disposition-schema/gotchas.md
#
# A repository-wide `* text=auto eol=lf` marks every one of them for
# renormalization at once. Measured on this branch: that makes `changeset status
# --since` report changed packages where none changed, which turned the
# spec-conformance poison control red - the control was correct and the rule was
# too wide for the change carrying it.
#
# Normalizing those ten is a real cleanup with its own diff and its own review.
# It is not part of consuming a prose style, so it is named here rather than done
# quietly under an unrelated ticket.
